hi this is pres Harker let's learn how  to play ultimate tic-tac-toe standard  tic-tac-toe is played on a 3x3 grid in  which each of two players alternates  placing X's and O's in squares the first  player to get three in a row wins the  game  ultimate tic-tac-toe is also played on a  3x3 grid but each of these squares also  has a 3x3 grid inside of it since each  3x3 grid has nine possible squares to  play this means this game has 81  different squares where you can place an  X or an O here are the rules of ultimate  tic-tac-toe the first player X can play  anywhere on the board so let's say X  plays in the center square in the upper  left-hand corner now o has to play in a  particular square since X played in the  upper left-hand corner that means o has  to play in the square corresponding to  the upper left-hand corner now since Oh  has played in the upper right-hand  corner X has to play somewhere in the  3x3 grid that's in the upper right-hand  corner and the game continues this way  each time one of the players plays that  forces which square the other player can  play in at some point you might get to a  place always just sent X to play in the  center square which is completely filled  if that happens  X can play in any of the squares so X  may decide to complete a three in a row  here and the play will continue with the  same rules  let's keep filling in the game the first  player to win three in a row in a  particular small game will win that game  and if a player happens to win three of  the games in a row  that's how you win ultimate tic-tac-toe  so you have to win the small square to  win the square and then you have to get  three of the squares in a row so it's a  pretty neat game you should give it a  try  and if people are interested I'll make a  video on how you can have a winning  strategy please subscribe to my channel  I make videos on math and game theory  you can support me on patreon catch me  on my blog mind your decisions on  Twitter at pressure Locker and you can  get my books at Amazon
 

